-- title:
--   Full original compensated H signed marked source isolates exactly one terminal ruin/horizon contact cell
-- statement:
--   For the source-identical H kernel of the actual original BV spectrally negative Lévy dividend process used by the published compensated HJB theorem, the genuine original global marked NX real integral equals the signed sum of the first m ruin/horizon clipped physical cells and one separate last stopped contact cell on the identical original Lévy path and admissible dividend strategy. Original BV H integrability is already discharged by accepted source-specific negative-mark variation certificates, so there is no extra integrability or stochastic hypothesis. The splitting applies the exact pinned Finset.sum_range_succ identity to the accepted original H finite-grid source theorem, maintaining the time-zero exclusion, original left-reserve and terminal contact.

import Mathlib.Analysis.Complex.Exponential
